            "body": "Message from claude: #5268 fixes the same OOM without shrinking the KV cache: it loads weights one FSDP module at a time, so a sync needs about one module extra instead of a second copy of the model. Reserving that copy at profiling costs a whole model of KV when the generator's FSDP degree is 1 (TP-only or 1-GPU generators). On one H100: Qwen3.5-9B TP1 KV cache 67.81 → 51.44 GiB, and Qwen3.5-35B-A3B TP1 fails to start (OOM in `profile_run`), while #5268 runs it with +1.6 GiB per sync. Only one of the two should land: with #5268, this hook would still reserve the full copy.\n",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-11T01:27:35Z",
            "databaseId": 6104190356,
            "updatedAt": "2026-10-11T01:27:35Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/5251#issuecomment-6104190356"
          },
          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "tianyu-l"
            },
            "body": "@felipemello1 \r\n\r\n> Only one of the two should land: with https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/5268, this hook would still reserve the full copy.\r\n\r\nmaybe impossible in reality, but technically even after your PR, the peak memory analysis is still more accurate with this change -- in the extremal case where a single FSDP module's shared param memory is more than all the peak activations",
            "createdAt": "2026-10-11T02:09:33Z",
            "databaseId": 6104487928,
            "updatedAt": "2026-10-11T02:09:33Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/5251#issuecomment-6104487928"
          }
