                  "body": "Thanks for capturing this. It seems a design limitation, which is exposed when `sharded_buffers` > `peak_activations`.\n- please add a comparison with the case when this `profile_run` override is not here, namely `unsharded_buffers + peak_activations` which underestimates actual memory usage outside KV cache\n- please add a NOTE / TODO about this limitation which we may want to revisit later.",
                  "createdAt": "2026-10-10T23:34:03Z",
                  "databaseId": 4239592866,
                  "diffHunk": "@@ -90,6 +90,28 @@ def load_model(self, load_dummy_weights: bool = False) -> None:\n             assert not self.cudagraph_dispatcher.keys_initialized\n             self.cudagraph_dispatcher = TorchTitanCudagraphDispatcher(self.vllm_config)\n \n+    def profile_run(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"\n+        Record weight sync buffers during vLLM's memory profiling.\n+\n+        vLLM sizes its KV cache by running model forward on dummy inputs to\n+        determine the transient peak memory. Here we simulate weight sync to\n+        ensure vLLM also takes into account the additional sharded buffers\n+        in its calculations, so we subtract the following from the KV cache:\n+\n+            unsharded_buffers + max(sharded_buffers, peak_activations)",
                  "line": 102,
                  "originalLine": 102,
                  "path": "torchtitan/rl/model/vllm_worker.py",
                  "updatedAt": "2026-10-10T23:34:05Z",
                  "url": "https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/5251#discussion_r4239592866"
                }
