  "files": [
    {
      "additions": 22,
      "blob_url": "https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/blob/dbd18384161040e6b21c134d2ec8d2a8fa8ee6d9/torchtitan%2Frl%2Fmodel%2Fvllm_worker.py",
      "changes": 22,
      "contents_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/pytorch/torchtitan/contents/torchtitan%2Frl%2Fmodel%2Fvllm_worker.py?ref=dbd18384161040e6b21c134d2ec8d2a8fa8ee6d9",
      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "torchtitan/rl/model/vllm_worker.py",
      "patch": "@@ -90,6 +90,28 @@ def load_model(self, load_dummy_weights: bool = False) -> None:\n             assert not self.cudagraph_dispatcher.keys_initialized\n             self.cudagraph_dispatcher = TorchTitanCudagraphDispatcher(self.vllm_config)\n \n+    def profile_run(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"\n+        Record weight sync buffers during vLLM's memory profiling.\n+\n+        vLLM sizes its KV cache by running model forward on dummy inputs to\n+        determine the transient peak memory. Here we simulate weight sync to\n+        ensure vLLM also takes into account the additional sharded buffers\n+        in its calculations, so we subtract the following from the KV cache:\n+\n+            unsharded_buffers + max(sharded_buffers, peak_activations)\n+\n+        This reflects the actual peak memory during RL training, since weight\n+        sync buffers and forward activations never appear at the same time.\n+        \"\"\"\n+        model = self.get_model()\n+        if hasattr(model, \"prepare_for_state_dict_load\") and hasattr(\n+            model, \"prepare_for_forward\"\n+        ):\n+            model.prepare_for_state_dict_load()\n+            model.prepare_for_forward()\n+        super().profile_run()\n+\n     def _pad_for_sequence_parallelism(self, num_scheduled_tokens: int) -> int:\n         tp_size = self.vllm_config.parallel_config.tensor_parallel_size\n         enable_dense_sp = self.compilation_config.pass_config.enable_sp and tp_size > 1",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/raw/dbd18384161040e6b21c134d2ec8d2a8fa8ee6d9/torchtitan%2Frl%2Fmodel%2Fvllm_worker.py",
      "sha": "c3d49866f26b70a621b4d543af46e30a87699b39",
      "status": "modified"
    }
  ],
  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "Thanks for capturing this. It seems a design limitation, which is exposed when `sharded_buffers` > `peak_activations`.\n- please add a comparison with the case when this `profile_run` override is not here, namely `unsharded_buffers + peak_activations` which underestimates actual memory usage outside KV cache\n- please add a NOTE / TODO about this limitation which we may want to revisit later.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-10T23:34:03Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -90,6 +90,28 @@ def load_model(self, load_dummy_weights: bool = False) -> None:\n             assert not self.cudagraph_dispatcher.keys_initialized\n             self.cudagraph_dispatcher = TorchTitanCudagraphDispatcher(self.vllm_config)\n \n+    def profile_run(self) -> None:\n+        \"\"\"\n+        Record weight sync buffers during vLLM's memory profiling.\n+\n+        vLLM sizes its KV cache by running model forward on dummy inputs to\n+        determine the transient peak memory. Here we simulate weight sync to\n+        ensure vLLM also takes into account the additional sharded buffers\n+        in its calculations, so we subtract the following from the KV cache:\n+\n+            unsharded_buffers + max(sharded_buffers, peak_activations)",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/5251#discussion_r4239592866",
      "id": 4239592866,
      "line": 102,
      "original_line": 102,
      "path": "torchtitan/rl/model/vllm_worker.py",
      "updated_at": "2026-10-10T23:34:05Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "tianyu-l"
      }
    }
  ],
  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "Message from claude: #5268 fixes the same OOM without shrinking the KV cache: it loads weights one FSDP module at a time, so a sync needs about one module extra instead of a second copy of the model. Reserving that copy at profiling costs a whole model of KV when the generator's FSDP degree is 1 (TP-only or 1-GPU generators). On one H100: Qwen3.5-9B TP1 KV cache 67.81 → 51.44 GiB, and Qwen3.5-35B-A3B TP1 fails to start (OOM in `profile_run`), while #5268 runs it with +1.6 GiB per sync. Only one of the two should land: with #5268, this hook would still reserve the full copy.\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-11T01:27:35Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/5251#issuecomment-6104190356",
      "id": 6104190356,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-11T01:27:35Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "felipemello1"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "@felipemello1 \r\n\r\n> Only one of the two should land: with https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/5268, this hook would still reserve the full copy.\r\n\r\nmaybe impossible in reality, but technically even after your PR, the peak memory analysis is still more accurate with this change -- in the extremal case where a single FSDP module's shared param memory is more than all the peak activations",
      "created_at": "2026-10-11T02:09:33Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/pytorch/torchtitan/pull/5251#issuecomment-6104487928",
      "id": 6104487928,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-11T02:09:33Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "tianyu-l"
      }
    }
  ],
